From 5a8d478eeab5c3a5df9c69e66c5a9bc22596c59e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:23:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] boss: Built-in SpotPass downloads

Without the BOSS module (online LLE off), SpotPass tasks never ran: StartTask and
StartTaskImmediate were stubs, and on a 3DS most tasks run in the background or in
sleep mode, which never happens in the emulator.

- StartTask/StartTaskImmediate download the task's URL on a worker thread (through
  the custom SpotPass server when enabled), decrypt the SpotPass container (key slot
  0x38) and store each payload in the game's SpotPass extdata, replacing older
  versions of the same NsData ID. Unchanged files are left alone.
- GetTaskState reports running (2), success (0) or failed (7). GetTaskStatus loads
  the task's properties, so the game can read the state, HTTP status, last success
  time and Last-Modified with ReceiveProperty.
- RegisterImmediateTask registers the task.
- With a custom SpotPass server set, each registered task runs once per Tangelo
  start, when the game opens its SpotPass session or registers the task.
- Downloaded files are "new" until the game clears the flag; the NsData new flag
  is kept per NsData ID. The new-arrival flag is set after a download.
- Task IDs are cut off at the first NUL, so tasks loaded from BOSS_SV.db match the
  ones the game registers.
- Running downloads stop when emulation stops.

